        },
        {
          "heading": "DITEMPA BUKAN DIBERI",
          "level": 1,
          "line": 2
        },
        {
          "heading": "PURPOSE: Standardized output format for geologist's petrophysical interpretation.",
          "level": 1,
          "line": 4
        },
        {
          "heading": "This template structures the FINAL DELIVERABLE — the interpretation that",
          "level": 1,
          "line": 5
        },
        {
          "heading": "goes into the well report, the reserves submission, or the geocellular model.",
          "level": 1,
          "line": 6
        },
        {
          "heading": "A petrophysics report is a CHAIN OF REASONING, not just a table of numbers.",
          "level": 1,
          "line": 8
        },
        {
          "heading": "Every number must be traceable to a measurement, a calibration, or an assumption.",
          "level": 1,
          "line": 9
        },
        {
          "heading": "CLAIM LIMITS: Every assumption must be stated explicitly with uncertainty bounds.",
          "level": 1,
          "line": 11
        },
        {
          "heading": "\"Porosity is estimated from density log with ±2 p.u. uncertainty at 1σ.\"",
          "level": 1,
          "line": 12
        },
        {
          "heading": "\"Water saturation uses Archie with m=2.0, n=2.0 — calibrated to core.\"",
          "level": 1,
          "line": 13
        },
        {
          "heading": "PHYSICS-9 RULE: The report must make the GENETIC STORY coherent with the NUMBERS.",
          "level": 1,
          "line": 15
        },
        {
          "heading": "GR motif, cross-plot, and log-derived properties must all tell the same story.",
